.Dd September 24, 2026
.Dt LISTEN 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm listen
.Nd listen for incoming connections on a socket
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn listen "int fd" "int backlog"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn listen
makes the stream socket
.Fa fd
passive and allocates a TCP control block in the
.Dv LISTEN
state.
Connections completed on it are queued for
.Xr accept 2 .
The operation is subcall 4 of i386
.Xr socketcall 2 ,
system call 102.
.Pp
The socket must have a nonzero local port assigned by
.Xr bind 2 .
This kernel does not assign a port at
.Fn listen .
Only one live listener may use a port.
A socket that is already listening or has any attached TCP control block
cannot be made a listener by another call.
Datagram and raw sockets do not support this operation.
.Pp
The kernel ignores
.Fa backlog .
Each listener has a 16-entry circular accept array, with one entry unused
to distinguish a full queue from an empty one.
It can queue at most 15 completed connections.
When the queue is full, a new connection request is refused with a TCP
reset before a connection is allocated.
The first such refusal is recorded in the kernel log; later refusals at
this check are not recorded.
If the queue fills while a handshake is completing, that connection is
closed and the queue refusal is logged.
Closing a listener frees the connections still in their handshake on its
port, with their sockets.
The peer's final acknowledgement then finds no connection: with no listener
on the port it is answered with a reset, and a listener opened on the port
since ignores it, so a connection begun under one listener is never
accepted by another.
.Pp
TCP control blocks are allocated from the kernel heap, with no fixed
pool size.
Failure to allocate the listener's control block returns
.Er ENOBUFS .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn listen
returns 0 on success, or -1 on failure and sets
.Va errno .
The kernel interface returns the negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/loopprobe.c
binds two stream sockets to the same port before either listens.
The first
.Fn listen
succeeds and the second returns
.Er EADDRINUSE .
The probe also checks that listening without a bound port returns
.Er EDESTADDRREQ .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EDESTADDRREQ]"
.It Bq Er EADDRINUSE
A live listener already uses the local port.
.It Bq Er EDESTADDRREQ
The socket has no nonzero local port.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The socketcall argument array cannot be read from user memory.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
The socket is already listening or has a TCP control block.
.It Bq Er ENOBUFS
The kernel could not allocate a TCP control block.
.It Bq Er ENOTSOCK
.Fa fd
is invalid or does not refer to a socket.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The socket is not a stream socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr accept 2 ,
.Xr bind 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr socketcall 2
